=== INVESTIGATION ===

Web page (web/src/features/vehicles/pages/VehicleAccessPage.tsx, 296 lines) is the
vehicle access manager: it lists the authorized drivers and the outstanding share
invitations for one vehicle, behind two independent TanStack sources, and offers the
mutations to keep both in sync. It is built from two `GlassPanel` regions inside a
`PageContainer`:
  • GlassPanel1 (Drivers) — header (Users icon + "Drivers" + count Badge + Refresh),
    then a `DataTable` of Name / Email / Role / [remove]. The remove action is shown
    only when `row.share_user_id != null`; it opens a danger `ConfirmDialog`.
  • GlassPanel2 (Invitations) — header (Mail icon + "Share Invitations" + count Badge
    + Refresh + "Invite Driver"), then a `DataTable` of Status / Created By / Expires /
    Link / [revoke]. Status maps to a `StatusBadge`
    (pending→'online', revoked→'offline', else→'asleep'); Link is a `CopyButton` when
    `invite_url` is present else '—'; Expires is a `TimeStamp`; revoke (shown only for
    `status === 'pending'`) opens a danger `ConfirmDialog`.

Data sources (8 hooks ported, web names kept at the Swift call site):
  useVehicle                  → GET    /vehicles/{id}                                  (breadcrumb label)
  useVehicleDrivers           → GET    /vehicles/{vehicleId}/drivers
  useVehicleInvitations       → GET    /vehicles/{vehicleId}/invitations
  useRefreshVehicleDrivers    → POST   /vehicles/{vehicleId}/drivers/refresh
  useRefreshVehicleInvitations→ POST   /vehicles/{vehicleId}/invitations/refresh
  useRemoveVehicleDriver      → DELETE /vehicles/{vehicleId}/drivers   (body share_user_id)
  useCreateVehicleInvitation  → POST   /vehicles/{vehicleId}/invitations
  useRevokeVehicleInvitation  → POST   /vehicles/{vehicleId}/invitations/{invitationId}/revoke

Manifest record (32 = 2 panels + 3 states + 27 strings):
  panels  : GlassPanel1 (Drivers), GlassPanel2 (Invitations)
  charts  : 0    maps : 0
  states  : loading, empty, success   (error ALSO implemented per source, ADR-011)
  strings : 27 vehicleAccess.* keys

